      "transcript": "Tell me about the rancho."
    },
    {
      "turnId": 2,
      "speaker": "A",
      "transcript": "Ay, okay. My grandfather's rancho, outside Jerez, in Zacatecas. Adobe house, one floor, long, like a line of rooms. You walk in through the portal, the porch, it runs the whole front of the house."
    },
    {
      "turnId": 3,
      "speaker": "B",
      "transcript": "What did the porch face?"
    },
    {
      "turnId": 4,
      "speaker": "A",
      "transcript": "The front of the house faced, um, east? Yes, east, because the sun came straight onto the portal in the morning and my grandfather sat there with his coffee."
    },
    {
      "turnId": 5,
      "speaker": "B",
      "transcript": "And the rooms?"
    },
    {
      "turnId": 6,
      "speaker": "A",
      "transcript": "From the portal there's a door into the sala, the main room, in the middle. The bedrooms were to the right of the sala, and the kitchen to the left. The kitchen had a fogón, a wood stove, built of adobe, against the back wall."
    },
    {
      "turnId": 7,
      "speaker": "B",
      "transcript": "Anything outside?"
    },
    {
      "turnId": 8,
      "speaker": "A",
      "transcript": "Behind the house, the corral, for the horses and some goats. And a well somewhere out back, I don't remember exactly where."
    },
    {
      "turnId": 9,
      "speaker": "B",
      "transcript": "Size of the house?"
    },
    {
      "turnId": 10,
      "speaker": "A",
      "transcript": "The portal was long, maybe sixty feet. The sala, you could fit twelve people eating in there, we did at Christmas."
    }
